{"book":7,"chapter":3,"context":{"chapter":3,"title":"Othniel, Ehud and Shamgar","summary":"God leaves some nations to test Israel. Othniel rescues Israel from a Mesopotamian king, the left-handed Ehud assassinates Eglon king of Moab, and Shamgar strikes down six hundred Philistines with an ox goad.","background":"Othniel's story (vv. 7–11) is the cycle at its simplest. The oppressor's name, Chushan-rishathaim, means 'Cushan of double wickedness,' probably a mocking label. Ehud was from Benjamin, a name meaning 'son of the right hand,' yet he was left-handed and carried his dagger on his right thigh (vv. 15–16), where a guard would not expect it.","customs":[{"term":"Covering his feet","verses":"3:24","note":"A polite way of saying someone is relieving himself. Eglon's servants assume this and wait outside, giving Ehud time to escape."},{"term":"Ox goad","verses":"3:31","note":"A long wooden stick, often metal-tipped, used to drive oxen while plowing; an improvised weapon."}],"watchFor":["'The Spirit of the Lord came upon him' (v. 10).","Ehud's 'message from God' (v. 20).","Seizing the fords of the Jordan cuts off the escape route (v. 28)."],"connections":["Joshua 15:16-17","Judges 5:6","Judges 20:16","1 Chronicles 12:2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וְאֵלֶּה","ve'eleh","H428","HC/Tm","and these"],["הַגּוֹיִם","hagoyim","H1471","HTd/Ncmpa","[are] the nations"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["הִנִּיחַ","hiniach","H5117","HVhp3ms","he left"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["לְנַסּוֹת","lenasot","H5254","HR/Vpcc","to put to [the] test"],["בָּם","bam","H9038","HRd/Sp3mp","by <the> them"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"],["אֵת","'et","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsa","all"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","[those] who"],["לֹא","lo'-","H3808","HTn","not"],["יָדְעוּ","yade'u","H3045","HVqp3cp","they had known"],["אֵת","'et","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","al